---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import TransformGenerator from '../../components/TransformGenerator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="CSS Transform Generator" description="Visually build a CSS transform — translate, rotate, scale, and skew — with live preview.">
  <TransformGenerator client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Why transform order matters</h2>
  <p>Multiple transform functions applied together are processed in the order they're written — rotating then translating produces a visually different result than translating then rotating, which trips up anyone assuming transforms combine order-independently.</p>

  <h2>How to use this generator</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Adjust translate, rotate, scale, and skew values with live preview.</li>
    <li>Copy the generated transform CSS property.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Assuming transform order doesn't matter</strong> — rotate-then-translate and translate-then-rotate produce different visual results, since each transform applies relative to the element's current transformed state.</li>
    <li><strong>Forgetting transform doesn't affect layout</strong> — a transformed element still occupies its original space in the document flow, which can surprise developers expecting it to behave like a position change.</li>
    <li><strong>Overusing transforms on many elements</strong> without considering rendering performance, especially with complex combined transforms animated simultaneously.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Creating a hover effect that scales or rotates an element</li>
    <li>Positioning an element precisely with translate for a design effect</li>
    <li>Building a card-flip or tilt interaction with combined transforms</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  <p><strong>Does transform affect other elements' layout?</strong> No — transform is purely visual; the element's original space in the document flow is preserved, unlike changing width/height/position which can shift surrounding content.</p>
</ToolLayout>
